$DIR/main.p:11:2: cannot store U.S{...} in package variable keep, which outlives in
    U.S{...} points into in. in is a local variable of f (declared at
    main.p:10). When f returns, in's memory is reclaimed, but package variables
    live for the whole program, so package variable keep would be left pointing
    at reclaimed memory.
    Go would move this memory to the heap, and its garbage collector would free
    it later. Plutonium has no garbage collector and never moves memory to the
    heap behind the program's back, so that every allocation is visible in the
    code.
    Store values instead of views of in, or allocate in and store its owner, an
    owned[Inner], which moves there:
        keep = new(Inner)
    (see "Views" in the Plutonium spec, section 18.3)
    (run "pluto explain E3002" for a longer explanation)
